# There is also no LICENSE file in the repository, so no `license:` field is
# declared here. Add one to both places together.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ADMET generalization: when does a graph neural network outperform a
  fingerprint-based model?
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/romazal/admet-generalization"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline comparing a Morgan-fingerprint random forest against
  a message-passing graph neural network on ADMET property prediction (Tox21,
  with ClinTox as a smaller second dataset). It tests two hypotheses: whether
  any GNN advantage survives a Bemis-Murcko scaffold split, and whether it
  depends on the amount of training data. Both models receive an equal
  hyperparameter budget, scaffold-disjointness is enforced and re-checked at
  run time, and every reported number regenerates from committed per-run
  result files.
keywords:
  - ADMET
  - molecular property prediction
  - graph neural network
  - molecular fingerprints
  - scaffold split
  - out-of-distribution generalization
  - Tox21
  - cheminformatics
